---
title: "claimTokenAllocation (LegionPreLiquidApprovedSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_paused: investor claims tokens
    q_check_paused --> q_check_supplied: not paused
    q_check_paused --> q_revert_paused: contract paused
    q_check_supplied --> q_check_not_claimed: tokens have been supplied
    q_check_supplied --> q_revert_supply: tokens not supplied
    q_check_not_claimed --> q_verify_alloc_sig: position.hasSettled == false
    q_check_not_claimed --> q_revert_claimed: already claimed
    q_verify_alloc_sig --> q_verify_vesting_sig: allocation signature valid (amount and rate)
    q_verify_alloc_sig --> q_revert_alloc: invalid allocation signature
    q_verify_vesting_sig --> q_check_vesting: vesting term signature valid
    q_verify_vesting_sig --> q_revert_vesting: invalid vesting signature
    q_check_vesting --> q_deploy_vesting: vestingTerms.duration > 0
    q_check_vesting --> q_direct_transfer: immediate allocation
    q_deploy_vesting --> q_transfer_vesting: deploy vesting contract via EIP-1167 clone
    q_transfer_vesting --> q_mark: transfer(vestingContract, tokenAmount)
    q_direct_transfer --> q_mark: transfer(investor, tokenAmount)
    q_mark --> [*]: position.hasSettled = true, emit TokensClaimed(investor, tokenAmount)
    q_revert_paused --> [*]: revert Paused
    q_revert_supply --> [*]: revert TokensNotSupplied
    q_revert_claimed --> [*]: revert AlreadyClaimed
    q_revert_alloc --> [*]: revert InvalidAllocationSignature
    q_revert_vesting --> [*]: revert InvalidVestingSignature

    note right of q_verify_alloc_sig
        INV-001: Dual signature verification - both allocation and vesting terms
        INV-002: Allocation amount derived from SAFT terms and actual investment
        INV-003: Vesting terms authorized separately for flexibility
    end note
